 information can be passed from one to the other. A gateway both transfers information and converts it to a form compatible with the protocols used by the receiving network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2026494">network gateway</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="465218">ປະຕູອອກ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1399_57949_2179357"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device that connects networks using different communications protocols so that information can be passed from one to the other. A gateway both transfers information and converts it to a form compatible with the protocols used by the receiving network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="57949">gateway</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2179357">ເກດເວ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1399_57949_465218"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A device that connects networks using different communications protocols so that information can be passed from one to the other. A gateway both transfers information and converts it to a form compatible with the protocols used by the receiving network.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="57949">gateway</term><termNote type="part