nated word, number, or phrase from breaking if it falls at the end of a line.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="85228">nonbreaking hyphen</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="465407">ຂີດຕໍ່ຄຳສັບ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3659_319140_466564"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ( character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="319140">opening parenthesis</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="466564">ເຄື່ອງໝາຍເປີດວົງເລັບ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="3662_77222_465350"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that makes the screen more readable by people who have low vision by creating a separate window that displays a magnified portion of the screen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="77222">Magnifier</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="465350">ແກ້ວຂະຫຍາຍ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36774_2070563_2115065"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A subset of settings and features that can be assigned to one of four slots in action center for quick, one-tap access. In addition, they can provide useful, actionable, or critical info regarding the setting or feature.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2070563">quick action</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2115065">ການດໍາເນີນການດ່ວນ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36775_2070564_2115198"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An app that is built using the Windows universal app platform. Developers can create a Windows universal app that runs on all Windows-based device types, or they can choose to limit an app to specific devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2070564">universal app</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2115198">ແອັບທົ່ວໄປ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36775_2247950_2115198"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An app that is built using the Windows universal app platform. Developers can create a Windows universal app that runs on all Windows-based device types, or they can choose to limit an app to specific devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2247950">Windows universal app</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2115198">ແອັບທົ່ວໄປ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36776_2070565_2114870"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To provide Wi-Fi credentials to Outlook.com contacts, Skype contacts, and Facebook friends.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2070565">exchange</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2114870">ແລກປ່ຽນ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36778_2071066_2114931"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The phone's volume mode when in a call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071066">In-Call</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2114931">ຢູ່ໃນການໂທ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36779_2071067_2114839"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The use of data connection in a roaming area. Generally making phone calls or using your data connection when the phone is roaming is more expensive, and the user will be charged additional fees for voice roaming calls.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071067">data roaming</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2114839">ການໂຣມມິງຂໍ້ມູນ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36780_2071068_2115223"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The connection on your phone that allows you to make phone calls.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071068">voice connection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2115223">ການເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ສຽງ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36781_2071069_2115226"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A phone call made in a roaming area. Generally making phone calls or using your data connection when the phone is roaming is more expensive, and the user will be charged additional fees for voice roaming calls.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071069">voice roaming</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2115226">ການໂຣມມິງສຽງ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36782_2238946_2114852"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The setting to minimize distractions while driving.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2238946">Driving mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2114852">ໂໝດຂັບຂີ່</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36783_2071243_2115093"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The setting that determines if the screen will rotate automatically when the phone is rotated.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071243">screen rotation</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2115093">ການໝຸນໜ້າຈໍ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36784_2071244_2115240"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft operating system designed for handheld portable devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071244">Windows Embedded Handheld</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2115240">Windows Embedded Handheld</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36785_2071245_2115239"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Microsoft operating system built on Windows Phone 8 designed for handheld portable devices.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071245">Windows Embedded 8 Handheld</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2115239">Windows Embedded 8 Handheld</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36786_2071246_2115167"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A predetermined text reply that can be automatically sent in response to incoming calls, text messages, or both when Driving Mode is turned on. The text reply is sent with no action on the part of the user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071246">text reply</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2115167">ການຕອບຄືນຂໍ້ຄວາມ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36787_2071247_2115168"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A response to an incoming call using a text message when the caller is a contact calling from a mobile phone.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071247">text reply</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2115168">ການຕອບຄືນຂໍ້ຄວາມ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36791_2071377_2115136"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A photo you can choose to use as the background for some Live Tiles on the Start screen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071377">Start background</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2115136">ພື້ນຫຼັງເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36792_2071378_2115218"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A Windows Phone feature to upgrade a phone call into a Skype video call.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071378">video upgrade</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2115218">ອັບເກຣດວິດີໂອ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36793_2071379_2115238"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A visual setting that enables app screen content to display in a window.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071379">windowed mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2115238">ໂໝດເປັນປ່ອງຢ້ຽມ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36794_2071380_2114871"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A visual setting that is similar to “stretch” - the resolution of the phone screen is refitted to fill as much of the external screen as possible without compromising its dimensionality.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071380">expanded screen mode</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2114871">ໂໝດໜ້າຈໍຂະຫຍາຍອອກ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36795_2071381_2115057"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Windows desktop application that is required to enable users to project their phone screen to a Windows device using a USB connection.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2071381">Project My Screen App</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2115057">ສາຍແອັບໜ້າຈໍຂອງຂ້ອຍ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36805_2072311_2163202"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that unifies components across applications, such as people, conversations, calendars, emails, and files, to create a seamless collaboration experience. Creating a group anywhere in Microsoft 365 will automatically provision a corresponding Yammer conversation feed, an Outlook inbox and calendar, and a SharePoint document library for every Group member. Groups make these components persistent across applications, so that changes made to components in part of Microsoft 365 will carry through to the others, thus enabling a unified experience.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2072311">Groups</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2163202">ກຸ່ມ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36805_2072311_2383169"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that unifies components across applications, such as people, conversations, calendars, emails, and files, to create a seamless collaboration experience. Creating a group anywhere in Microsoft 365 will automatically provision a corresponding Yammer conversation feed, an Outlook inbox and calendar, and a SharePoint document library for every Group member. Groups make these components persistent across applications, so that changes made to components in part of Microsoft 365 will carry through to the others, thus enabling a unified experience.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2072311">Groups</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2383169">ກຸ່ມ Office 365</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36805_2874478_2163202"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that unifies components across applications, such as people, conversations, calendars, emails, and files, to create a seamless collaboration experience. Creating a group anywhere in Microsoft 365 will automatically provision a corresponding Yammer conversation feed, an Outlook inbox and calendar, and a SharePoint document library for every Group member. Groups make these components persistent across applications, so that changes made to components in part of Microsoft 365 will carry through to the others, thus enabling a unified experience.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2874478">Microsoft 365 Groups</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2163202">ກຸ່ມ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36805_2874478_2383169"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature that unifies components across applications, such as people, conversations, calendars, emails, and files, to create a seamless collaboration experience. Creating a group anywhere in Microsoft 365 will automatically provision a corresponding Yammer conversation feed, an Outlook inbox and calendar, and a SharePoint document library for every Group member. Groups make these components persistent across applications, so that changes made to components in part of Microsoft 365 will carry through to the others, thus enabling a unified experience.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2874478">Microsoft 365 Groups</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2383169">ກຸ່ມ Office 365</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36806_2072312_2302512"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The database that stores search feature settings which include but are not limited to query rules and the search schema.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2072312">search settings database</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2302512">ຖານຂໍ້ມູນການຕັ້ງຄ່າການຊອກຫາ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36807_2072313_2302504"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature that enables the user to record on-screen activity, and embeds the video automatically in PowerPoint.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2072313">Screen Recording</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2302504">ການບັນທຶກໜ້າຈໍ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36832_2085426_2302200"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A menu that contains the most commonly used contextual commands such as Cut, Copy, Paste, Comment, and Proofing.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2085426">Mini Toolbar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2302200">ແຖບເຄື່ອງມືຂະໜາດນ້ອຍ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36833_2085429_2163279"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A yellow bar with a warning icon appearing below the ribbon that provides information or alerts the user. Information can be security alerts, errors, or notifications.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2085429">Message Bar</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2163279">ແຖບ​ຂໍ້​ຄວາມ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36834_2085430_2302393"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A dialog box that shows the progress of an operation.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2085430">Progress UI</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2302393">UI ຄວາມຄືບໜ້າ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36835_2085431_2301774"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A recurring meeting that does not have a standard pattern of daily, weekly, monthly, etc.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2085431">custom repeat</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2301774">ການເຮັດຊໍ້າແບບກຳນົດເອງ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36836_2086047_2301598"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The icon on the upper-left corner of the Office 365 suite. The icon is the entry point to all Office 365 services for which the user has a valid subscription, and to the Admin center (only if the user is an admin).</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2086047">app launcher</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2301598">ໂຕເປີດແອັບ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36872_2093287_2302761"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature of OneNote for Android that allows you to create notes, audio notes, and picture notes right from your phone’s home screen.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2093287">widget</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2302761">ວິດເຈັດ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="36873_2093298_2301751"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A contextual tab on the Ribbon that enables the user to modify the appearance, size, and other aspects of the container controls in a form.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2093298">Control Tools</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></te