o/image on top of a larger video/image in a video editing project.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060438">picture-in-picture</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3067096">ຮູບຊ້ອນຮູບ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53750_3060439_3064019"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The feature in Clipchamp that increases or reduces the playback speed of a video or audio track.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060439">Clip speed</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3064019">ຄວາມໄວຄລິບ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="53751_3060440_3067093"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of motion text title or graphic that covers the lower region of the video frame, often used in TV broadcasting.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3060440">lower third</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3067093">ສ່ວນລຸ່ມໜຶ່ງໃນສາມ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote 