key is used to generate the client-read key, the client-write key, the server-read key, and the server-write key. Master keys can be exported as simple key BLOBs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="78635">master key</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="465365">ລະຫັດແມ່</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7870_232418_2302507"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A search folder created in Outlook that provides a view of all email items matching specific search criteria and where the items are still stored in one or more Outlook folder.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="232418">Search Folders</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2302507">ຊອກຫາໂຟນເດີ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7874_7041_464830"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A string of characters entered by a user to verify his or her identity to a network or to a local computer, device, or client, or to sign in to an account, app, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7041">access code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="464830">ລະຫັດເຂົ້າຫາ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7874_7041_464831"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A string of characters entered by a user to verify his or her identity to a network or to a local computer, device, or client, or to sign in to an account, app, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7041">access code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="464831">ລະຫັດຜ່ານ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7874_7042_464830"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A string of characters entered by a user to verify his or her identity to a network or to a local computer, device, or client, or to sign in to an account, app, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7042">password</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="464830">ລະຫັດເຂົ້າຫາ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7874_7042_464831"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A string of characters entered by a user to verify his or her identity to a network or to a local computer, device, or client, or to sign in to an account, app, and so on.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="7042">password</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="464831">ລະຫັດຜ່ານ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7875_307417_2301623"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A technology that allows Outlook and mobile devices to automatically discover and connect to the correct Exchange server without requiring the user to know the Exchange server name or other details, even if the mailbox has been moved or a server has failed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="307417">AutoConnect</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2301623">ເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ອັດຕະໂນມັດ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7878_236973_2179772"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature of Parental Controls that allows users to block Web sites that they don't want to view.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="236973">Web restrictions</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2179772">ການຈໍາກັດເວັບ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7878_236973_466137"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A feature of Parental Controls that allows users to block Web sites that they don't want to view.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="236973">Web restrictions</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Plural</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="466137">ເວັບທີ່ຕ້ອງຫ້າມ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7885_48295_465155"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To move an item on the screen (1) by touching the item on a screen and then sliding the finger across the screen or (2) by pressing and holding down the left mouse button while moving the mouse.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="48295">drag</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="lo"><ntig><termGrp><term id="465155">ລາກ</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">LAO</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="7904_234775_466098"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Visual impairment that results in great reduction in vision capabilities and that cannot be aided by glasses or contact lenses. It could, howev